    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1441">

                <pb facs="1153" n="1143" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.9532: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawthorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-07T10:00:00+08:00">September 7,
                            1949—10 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 7—8:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>481. Re mytels 316, July 5, reporting loss fuel stockpile, 394, July 30 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">August 3</hi>], reporting certain present and
                    anticipated difficulties of ConGen, and 459, August 30, re Communists’ attitude
                    toward ITS Government property.</p>
                <p>Believe it will be impossible obtain fuel for office and residences for coming
                    winter absence some sort recognition or agreement on high level, if factories
                    given preference in purchasing fuel. Any case diesel will not be available for
                    heating ConGen and house at 1 First Taiping <pb facs="1154" n="1144"
                        xml:id="pg1144"/> Church Road and heating systems these properties must be
                    converted to coal, but Department seems reluctant grant even $100 for repair
                    upkeep Government buildings (see mytel 356, July 21<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d1441-f1"/> which, together with all other telegrams requesting
                    additional funds, remains unanswered). Without such recognition or agreement
                    believe US Government properties will be taken over in not distant future. Also
                    that it will continue to be impossible for ConGen contact any responsible
                    Communist official [garble] departure Americans who have resigned or have been
                    granted premature home leave. Owing present conditions, American business
                    community will consist of 4 men, none representing American firms.</p>
                <p>Morale my American staff suffering from general feeling frustration, shared by
                    me, departures personnel other friends and narrowing recreational
                    facilities.</p>
                <p>Department pass Nanking its discretion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawthorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
